; TEST: expect-exit=100
;
; A reduction with NO CONTRIBUTION yields the op's identity -- in both
; shapes, and that is the half of the definition which makes the rest
; consistent (ssa-ir.md 2.6, as defined 2026-09-25). `redinit` immediately
; followed by `redfin` is legal IR: rule 5 asks that every `contrib` be
; dominated by its `redinit` and that `redfin` post-dominate every `contrib`
; of its handle, and zero contributions satisfy both vacuously.
;
;   1  fadd f32,  ordinata     = +0.0   0x00000000
;   2  mul  i64,  ordinata     = 1      (NOT 0 -- the multiplicative identity)
;   3  add  u32,  arborea 8    = 0      count never reaches w, tail is empty
;   4  fmul f64,  arborea 4    = 1.0    0x3FF0000000000000
;
; CHECKS 3 AND 4 ARE THE `arborea` TAIL AT k = 0. `redfin`'s tail dispatch
; reads the live count, finds 0, and jumps straight to its join without
; folding anything -- so the accumulator is still the identity it was given
; by `redinit`. A lowering that folded slots[0] unconditionally would read a
; cell nothing ever wrote (the frame's fourth region is not zeroed) and
; answer garbage; this fixture is what makes that loud rather than
; intermittent.
;
; Check 2 is why `mul`'s identity has to be a separate case in
; __bfa_red_ident: 0 would make every product 0, and the bug would be
; invisible in any fixture that happened to contribute a 0.
;
; Mutation (run): one identity table for every op (0) -> exit 2 and exit 4.
; `redfin` folding the tail unconditionally -> exit 3 or 4, nondeterministically
; (whatever the frame held).
;
; CROSS-CHECKED THROUGH THE C BACKEND, 2026-09-27. This fixture carried
; `c-emit-exit=4` from the day it landed: the C backend refused the three
; reduction opcodes, so the differential phase could only check parity of a
; refusal. It carries the key no longer -- `backend_c/emit_c.inc` lowers
; `redinit`/`contrib`/`redfin`, and the four builds (gcc and clang, -O0 and
; -O2, every one under `-fsanitize=undefined -fno-sanitize-recover=all`) are
; held to the SAME directive above as the reference's own run. The reference's
; verdict here is unchanged and has been since the day it landed; what is new
; is that three more toolchains have to agree with it.
;
; What this one cross-checks in particular: the `arborea` tail at k = 0. The
; C lowering's tail is an `else if` chain on the live count, so "count 0 folds
; nothing" is a chain no arm of which matches, where the reference's is a
; compare-and-jump chain that falls through to its join. Two different shapes,
; and checks 3 and 4 require them to answer the same identity.

functio @initium (ptr) -> u8 {
b0:
%0 = param ptr 0
%1 = slot 8 8
%2 = redinit f32 fadd ordinata 0
%3 = redfin f32 %2
store f32 %1 0 nativus %3
%4 = load u32 %1 0 nativus
%5 = iconst u32 0
%6 = cmp.eq u32 %4 %5
br %6 b2 b1
b1:
%7 = iconst u8 1
ret %7
b2:
%8 = redinit i64 mul ordinata 0
%9 = redfin i64 %8
%10 = iconst i64 1
%11 = cmp.eq i64 %9 %10
br %11 b4 b3
b3:
%12 = iconst u8 2
ret %12
b4:
%13 = redinit u32 add arborea 8
%14 = redfin u32 %13
%15 = iconst u32 0
%16 = cmp.eq u32 %14 %15
br %16 b6 b5
b5:
%17 = iconst u8 3
ret %17
b6:
%18 = redinit f64 fmul arborea 4
%19 = redfin f64 %18
store f64 %1 0 nativus %19
%20 = load u64 %1 0 nativus
%21 = iconst u64 4607182418800017408
%22 = cmp.eq u64 %20 %21
br %22 b8 b7
b7:
%23 = iconst u8 4
ret %23
b8:
%24 = iconst u8 100
ret %24
}
